Summary:
## 1. Primary Request and Intent

**Original (earlier segments, now complete):** Rebuild dhruv2mars.com from scratch in Chan Dai's (dai.is-a.dev, github.com/ncdai/chanhdai.com) design idiom with our own information architecture. Delivered as 7 commits on branch `feat/dai-idiom-rebuild`, draft PR **https://github.com/Dhruv2mars/portfolio/pull/36**.

**User's rejection of that work (pivotal turn):** The site "does not at all look like Chan dai's. It feels like as if someone has tried to copy from their own imagination without making sure that each and every part and detail are done exactly perfectly. There are so many things that are wrong, incomplete, or just inconsistent, which makes it look like a cheap copy by a five-year-old rather than an exact front end." They instructed me to spawn a single subagent (sonnet, low reasoning) that shells out to `codex` with `gpt-5.6-luna` at high reasoning to act as a fidelity critic.

**Follow-up correction:** "no, u should use sonnet with low reasoning effort in the subagent!" — Agent tool has no `effort` param; user chose "Respawn via Workflow" from AskUserQuestion so `agent({model:'sonnet', effort:'low'})` could be literally set.

**CURRENT TASK (most recent user turn, verbatim):** "Do all of them, complete each and every part, including the polish and optional ones. Make sure that the entire website is fully done and done with other details. Once you are done, then use the same subagent workflow critic to do the review again. by comparing our version (draft pr preview in browser) and chan dai's site in browser, using computer use."

So: implement **all 22 items** from the critic's plan (8 must-fix + 9 polish + 5 optional), then re-run the same Workflow critic doing a **browser-based visual comparison** (PR preview vs dai.is-a.dev) using computer use.

## 2. Key Technical Concepts

- Next.js 16.2.10 App Router (Turbopack), React 19, TypeScript 5.8, Tailwind CSS v4, bun 1.3.13
- Tailwind v4 `@utility` directive (Chan Dai's mechanism for `screen-line-top`, `stripe-divider`, `diagonal-stripes`, `link-underline`, `extend-touch-target`), `@theme inline`, `@custom-variant dark (&:where(.dark, .dark *))`
- `screen-line-top/bottom`: `::before/::after` with `absolute top-0 left-[-100vw] -z-1 h-px w-[200vw] bg-line` — viewport-spanning hairlines
- `--line: color-mix(in oklab, var(--border) 64%, var(--background))` — the token our build lacks entirely
- Zinc-based oklch token system (NOT blue accent)
- `next-themes`, `document.startViewTransition`, `useSyncExternalStore(noSubscribe, () => true, () => false)` as lint-clean hydration hook
- `react-hooks/refs` lint rule: reading a ref inside a `useCallback` referenced from JSX during render is an error
- `next-mdx-remote/rsc` + `rehype-sanitize` + `sugar-high`; `@vercel/blob` for AI activity
- Listbox pattern (`role="listbox"`/`role="option"`/`aria-activedescendant`) for 365 heatmap cells as one tab stop
- WCAG 2.5.8 24×24 targets, with calendar-grid essential-presentation exception
- `codex exec -m gpt-5.6-luna -c model_reasoning_effort=high -s danger-full-access --skip-git-repo-check -C <dir> --add-dir <dir> -o <file>` (codex-cli 0.147.0)
- Workflow tool `agent(prompt, {label, model, effort, phase, schema})`

