content.text:
This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent:**

   The user's active instruction (verbatim, their most recent substantive message): **"Do all of them, complete each and every part, including the polish and optional ones. Make sure that the entire website is fully done and done with other details. Once you are done, then use the same subagent workflow critic to do the review again. by comparing our version (draft pr preview in browser) and chan dai's site in browser, using computer use."** followed by **"continue....keep going"**.

   Both halves are now discharged: all 22 items from the round-1 critic's plan were implemented, committed, and pushed; the round-2 Workflow critic ran and returned **80/100** (up from 23/100). The natural continuation — and what I am mid-way through — is acting on the round-2 verdict's 4 must-fixes and 6 polish items, in the same "do all of them, including the polish" spirit.

   Background intent: rebuild dhruv2mars.com in Chan Dai's (dai.is-a.dev / github.com/ncdai/chanhdai.com) design idiom with our own information architecture. Work lives on branch `feat/dai-idiom-rebuild`, draft PR **https://github.com/Dhruv2mars/portfolio/pull/36**. The user's original complaint was that the prior attempt "feels like as if someone has tried to copy from their own imagination without making sure that each and every part and detail are done exactly perfectly" — so every change is made against **observed** Chan Dai source or **measured** browser state, never from memory.

2. **Key Technical Concepts:**
   - Next.js 16.2.10 App Router (Turbopack), React 19, TypeScript 5.8, Tailwind CSS v4, bun 1.3.13, `geist` 1.7.2
   - Tailwind v4 `@utility`, `@theme inline`, `@custom-variant dark (&:where(.dark, .dark *))`
   - `screen-line-top/bottom`: `::before/::after` with `absolute top-0 left-[-100vw] -z-1 h-px w-[200vw] bg-line` — viewport-spanning hairlines. Note: these make an element's `scrollWidth` ≈ 2× viewport, which is expected and must not be mistaken for overflow.
   - `--line: color-mix(in oklab, var(--border) 64%, var(--background))`
   - Tailwind arbitrary-variant chaining: `max-sm:*:data-[slot=command-menu-trigger]:hidden` (Chan Dai's own idiom for hiding a child by data-slot below `sm`)
   - Isometric SVG geometry from one `EDGE` constant: `HALF_W = EDGE*√3/2`, `HALF_H = EDGE/2`; painter's algorithm via background-filled side faces instead of depth sorting
   - SVG `<pattern patternTransform="rotate(-30)">` for hatch fills; fixed pattern id is acceptable in a server component rendered once
   - `next-themes` with `enableSystem`; **this version has no `fallback` prop**
   - **RSC boundary rule:** a `"use client"` module's exports are *client references* on the server — shared constants must live in a neutral module (why `LEVEL_ALPHA` lives in `lib/activity-grid.ts`)
   - `next-mdx-remote/rsc` + `rehype-sanitize` + `sugar-high`; `@vercel/blob` for AI activity
   - Listbox pattern (`role="listbox"`/`role="option"`/`aria-activedescendant`) for 365 heatmap cells as one tab stop
   - `codex exec -m gpt-5.6-luna -c model_reasoning_effort=high --yolo --skip-git-repo-check -C <dir> --add-dir <dir> -o <file>` (codex-cli 0.147.0). `--yolo` required for browser driving; must NOT be paired with `--full-auto`
   - Workflow tool `agent(prompt, {label, model, effort, phase, schema})` — the **only** way to set reasoning effort on a subagent
   - `agent-browser` CLI: `--session <name>`, `open`, `eval`, `screenshot`, and **`set viewport <w> <h>`** (bare `viewport` is not a command)
   - `lib/utils.ts` `cn()` is a **plain filter+join, no tailwind-merge** — conflicting Tailwind classes resolve by CSS source order
   - Vercel SSO deployment protection (`ssoProtection.deploymentType: "all_except_custom_domains"`); "Protection Bypass for Automation" is plan-gated

3. **Files and Code Sections:**

   **`/tmp/critique/round2/verdict.md`** (383B, written by codex) — the pointer file:
   ```
   Done. Real headed-browser audit complete.
   - OURS used: `http://localhost:3001/` — preview hit Vercel SSO.
   - Verdict: **80/100**
   - Report: [report.md](/tmp/critique/round2/report.md)
   - 16 required screenshots + interaction captures saved under `/tmp/critique/round2/`.
   - No source edits; repo clean.
   - Could not verify preview equivalence or reference heatmap keyboard semantics.
   ```

   **`/tmp/critique/round2/report.md`** — the full round-2 critique. Header: `VERDICT: 80/100 — strong frame-system and list-row match; hero construction, mobile overflow, and footer craft keep it from feeling fully Chan Dai.` Used localhost:3001 (Vercel preview redirected to a login wall; did not log in). Could not check: preview equivalence; reference heatmap keyboard traversal (his contribution graphic exposes no focusable grid/listbox semantics). Checked in headed Chromium at 1440×900 and 390×844, light and dark.

   **Must-fix (4):**
   1. At 390px, collapse or reflow the header nav — `activity`/`work` plus search/GitHub/theme exceed the viewport; theme control visibly cut off at right. Match reference mobile behavior: logo plus compact controls.
   2. Remove mobile heatmap horizontal overflow (scrollbar under the grid at 390px) — make cells/labels fit or provide intentional contained scrolling without page-level spill.
   3. Reconnect hero art to frame language — his hero diagonals, rails, and hatched line-art form one construction; ours is a solid cube floating centered in empty space.
   4. Fix bottom separator composition — two adjacent diagonal-stripe bands after the last project before footer; collapse to one.

   **Polish (6):** (1) denser footer rhythm — ruled cells / aligned metadata columns; (2) vary project icon tiles or use semantic per-project marks (repeated cube reads template-like); (3) tune mobile hero density — monogram tile much smaller than reference portrait slot; (4) match desktop nav casing/weight (ours lowercase and lighter vs his compact title-case); (5) normalize focus-ring treatment across header buttons, palette, links, heatmap; (6) restore a small authored micro-detail in hero or section notes.

   **What ours already gets right (7):** centered rails + edge-to-edge hairlines + diagonal bands; disciplined neutral light/dark palette with no stray accent; project row anatomy (icon tile, dashed inner rule, stack, chips, trailing affordance, separators, restrained hover); sans/mono pairing and small metadata labels; sticky header, theme toggle, command palette, Escape close, focus ring, heatmap arrow traversal all working; truthful product choices reading as craft (monogram + `portrait pending`, hidden empty blog, `feed stalled` caption); calm motion.

   **`components/site-header.tsx`** — EDITED. Two changes:
   ```tsx
   {/* Below `sm` the bar collapses to mark plus controls. The nav targets
       are in-page anchors on a single scroll, so losing them costs
       nothing, and keeping them cost the theme toggle its right gutter. */}
   <nav
     aria-label={FOCUSABLE_CHROME.primaryNavLabel}
     className="flex items-center max-sm:hidden"
   >
   ```
   ```tsx
   {/* The palette trigger is a keyboard affordance; a touch viewport has
       no ⌘K, so it goes with the nav. */}
   <div className="flex items-center max-sm:*:data-[slot=command-menu-trigger]:hidden">
   ```
   (`PaletteTrigger` in `components/command-palette.tsx:257` already carries `data-slot="command-menu-trigger"`.)

   **`app/page.tsx`** — EDITED. Removed the trailing divider:
   ```tsx
       <PanelDivider />
       <ProjectsSection />
       {/* No trailing divider. Bands go *between* panels; the footer opens with
           its own, and two adjacent bands read as a double border. */}
     </div>
   ```

   **`components/activity-grid.tsx`** — EDITED:
   ```ts
   /**
    * 26 columns is what fits a 390px viewport without a scrollbar:
    * 26×12px + 25×2px + the grid's 2px inline padding = 366px inside a 372px rail.
    */
   const MOBILE_WEEKS = 26;
   ```

   **`app/globals.css`** — EDITED, two changes in the activity mosaic block:
   ```css
   .activity-grid {
     --cell-size: 12px;
     --cell-gap: 2px;
     display: grid;
     grid-template-columns: repeat(var(--weeks, 53), var(--cell-size));
     gap: var(--cell-gap);
     width: max-content;
     max-width: 100%;
     margin-inline: auto;
     outline: none;
     /* Room for the focus outline's 1px offset and the live cell's 2px ring, so
        neither can cross the panel's vertical rail. */
     padding-inline: 2px;
   }
   ```
   and in `@media (max-width: 40rem)`: `grid-template-columns: repeat(var(--weeks-sm, 26), var(--cell-size));`

   **`components/site-mark.tsx`** — HEAVILY EDITED. `SiteMark` (header cube), `Cube`, `Cell`, `origin`, `points`, `round`, `EDGE`/`HALF_W`/`HALF_H` all kept. Removed `sorted()`, `FIGURE`, and an interim `ground()`/`FloorPlane`. New Fig. 1:
   ```tsx
   /* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
      Fig. 1 — the hero construction.

      Drawn, not rendered: faces are outlined and hatched rather than filled with
      tone, and the floor lattice runs off every edge of the plate to be cut there.
      That is the frame's own habit — a line is stopped by the viewport, never
      tidied to fit — and it is what keeps the figure attached to the page instead
      of floating on it.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------- */

   /** Corner (i, j) of the cell lattice, raised by `lift` edge-lengths. */
   function corner(i: number, j: number, lift: number): [number, number] {
     return [(i - j) * HALF_W, (i + j) * HALF_H - lift * EDGE];
   }

   /** Footprint is inclusive on both axes; `thick` and `lift` are in edge-lengths. */
   type Slab = { x0: number; y0: number; x1: number; y1: number; lift: number; thick: number };

   /**
    * Three platforms stepping down toward the viewer. Authored back-to-front:
    * side faces are painted with the page background, so each slab occludes the
    * one behind it without any depth sorting.
    */
   const SLABS: readonly Slab[] = [
     { x0: 0, y0: 0, x1: 3, y1: 1, lift: 1.2, thick: 0.4 },
     { x0: 2, y0: 2, x1: 7, y1: 3, lift: 0.6, thick: 0.4 },
     { x0: 5, y0: 4, x1: 11, y1: 5, lift: 0, thick: 0.4 },
   ];

   function SlabShape({ slab }: { slab: Slab }) {
     const { x0, y0, x1, y1, lift, thick } = slab;
     const back = corner(x0, y0, lift);
     const right = corner(x1 + 1, y0, lift);
     const front = corner(x1 + 1, y1 + 1, lift);
     const left = corner(x0, y1 + 1, lift);
     const drop = thick * EDGE;
     const down = ([x, y]: [number, number]): [number, number] => [x, y + drop];

     return (
       <g stroke="currentColor" strokeWidth={0.6} strokeLinejoin="round">
         <polygon points={points([left, front, down(front), down(left)])} fill="var(--background)" strokeOpacity={0.55} />
         <polygon points={points([front, right, down(right), down(front)])} fill="var(--background)" strokeOpacity={0.35} />
         <polygon points={points([back, right, front, left])} fill="url(#site-mark-hatch)" strokeOpacity={0.7} />
       </g>
     );
   }

   /** Generous enough that every line leaves the viewBox rather than ending in it. */
   const FLOOR = { lo: -8, hi: 20, centre: 6 };

   function FloorLattice() {
     const lines: Array<[[number, number], [number, number], number]> = [];
     for (let n = FLOOR.lo; n <= FLOOR.hi; n += 1) {
       // Fade with distance from the figure so the cut ends are already faint.
       const fade = Math.max(0, 1 - Math.abs(n - FLOOR.centre) / (FLOOR.hi - FLOOR.lo) / 0.55);
       if (fade === 0) continue;
       lines.push([corner(FLOOR.lo, n, -0.4), corner(FLOOR.hi, n, -0.4), fade]);
       lines.push([corner(n, FLOOR.lo, -0.4), corner(n, FLOOR.hi, -0.4), fade]);
     }
     return (
       <g stroke="currentColor" strokeWidth={0.5}>
         {lines.map(([[x1, y1], [x2, y2], fade], i) => (
           <line key={i} x1={round(x1)} y1={round(y1)} x2={round(x2)} y2={round(y2)}
                 strokeOpacity={round(0.16 * fade)} />
         ))}
       </g>
     );
   }

   export function SiteMarkIsometric({ className, ...props }: React.ComponentProps<"svg">) {
     return (
       <svg viewBox="-193 -34 490 232" className={cn("text-foreground", className)} aria-hidden="true" {...props}>
         <defs>
           {/* Hatching on the 30° axis, so the shading is made of the same lines
               as everything else on the page. */}
           <pattern id="site-mark-hatch" width="5" height="5" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse" patternTransform="rotate(-30)">
             <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="5" stroke="currentColor" strokeWidth="0.6" strokeOpacity="0.3" />
           </pattern>
         </defs>
         <FloorLattice />
         {SLABS.map((slab) => (
           <SlabShape key={`${slab.x0}-${slab.y0}-${slab.lift}`} slab={slab} />
         ))}
       </svg>
     );
   }
   ```

   **`components/profile-header.tsx`** — EDITED (one line):
   ```tsx
   {/* Sized to overflow the plate a little; the grid's `overflow-y-clip`
       cuts it, which is the point. */}
   <SiteMarkIsometric className="h-44 w-full sm:h-60" />
   ```

   **`components/site-footer.tsx`** — READ, not yet edited. Current shape: `<footer className="max-w-screen overflow-x-clip px-2">` → `<div className="mx-auto border-x border-line md:max-w-3xl">` → `screen-line-top screen-line-bottom` wrapper holding `stripe-divider h-12` → a `COLOPHON` `dl` with `grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-x-4 gap-y-2 px-4 py-3 font-mono`, `dt` = `text-right text-[0.625rem]/5 tracking-wider text-muted-foreground uppercase`, `dd` = `text-sm/5` → social icon band → `pb-[env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0)]`. `COLOPHON` currently has 3 entries (site, stack, source) plus a `©` row.

   **`/tmp/critique/dai/site-footer.tsx`** — READ for reference. His differences: `dl` is `flex flex-col gap-4 py-8 font-mono [&_dd]:text-sm [&_dt]:text-right [&_dt]:text-sm [&_dt]:text-muted-foreground [&_ul]:flex [&_ul]:flex-col [&_ul]:gap-2`; each row is `function Item = grid grid-cols-2 gap-4` (two **equal** columns, dt right-aligned in the left half); `dt` labels are sentence-case ("Crafted by", "Inspired by", "Deployed on", "Analytics", "Source code", "License") not uppercase micro-caps; several `dd`s hold multi-`li` `ul`s giving real density; a `Separator` (`flex h-11 w-px bg-line`) sits between **every** social icon, not just before the last.

   **`/tmp/critique/dai/home-page.tsx`** — READ. Decisive evidence for must-fix #4: the page ends `<Sponsors />` with **no trailing `<Separator />`**. His `Separator` is `stripe-divider h-(--separator-height) w-full border-x border-line`, identical to our `PanelDivider`.

   **`/tmp/critique/dai/site-header.tsx`** — READ. His logo is mark-only (no wordmark text); controls div carries `max-sm:*:data-[slot=command-menu-trigger]:hidden`; nav component is literally named `NavDesktop`.

   **`lib/projects.ts`** — READ. 8 projects with `{name, description, url, live?, language, year, note?}`: relunar (TS, npm), pi-queue (TS, npm), offdex (TS), gunmetal (Rust), mdv-ts (TS), block (TS), codexchat (Rust), openutm-v0 (TS). Exports `getProjects()`, `PROJECT_NAMES`, `destinationHost()`. No `kind`/icon field yet — this is where per-project glyphs would be wired for polish #2.

   **`components/projects-section.tsx`** — READ. Every row renders the same `<IconTile className="mx-4"><BoxIcon /></IconTile>` — the source of polish #2's "repeated cube reads template-like".

