This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent:**

   The user's standing instruction (verbatim, from before this segment): **"Do all of them, complete each and every part, including the polish and optional ones. Make sure that the entire website is fully done and done with other details. Once you are done, then use the same subagent workflow critic to do the review again. by comparing our version (draft pr preview in browser) and chan dai's site in browser, using computer use."** Followed by **"continue....keep going"**, and in this segment: **"keep going! and continue"** and **"continue whats left and keep going!!!"**.

   Background intent: rebuild dhruv2mars.com in Chan Dai's (dai.is-a.dev / github.com/ncdai/chanhdai.com) design idiom with our own information architecture. Work lives on branch `feat/dai-idiom-rebuild`, draft PR **https://github.com/Dhruv2mars/portfolio/pull/36**. The user's original complaint was that the prior attempt "feels like as if someone has tried to copy from their own imagination without making sure that each and every part and detail are done exactly perfectly" — so every change is made against **observed** Chan Dai source or **measured** browser state, never from memory.

   Status: all 4 must-fixes and all 6 polish items from the round-2 critic (80/100) are now implemented, verified in-browser, gated, committed (`ecb06aa`) and pushed. The round-3 critic was launched and **failed to actually run** — that is the live problem.

2. **Key Technical Concepts:**
   - Next.js 16.2.10 App Router (Turbopack), React 19, TypeScript 5.8, Tailwind CSS v4, bun 1.3.13
   - Tailwind v4 `@utility`, `@theme inline`, `@custom-variant`. New this segment: `@custom-variant pointer-fine (@media (pointer: fine));`
   - `screen-line-top/bottom` utilities apply `relative` — so `Panel` is already a positioning context (needed for the margin note)
   - SVG `preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice"` to make a drawing *cover* its box and be cut at the edges, instead of the default `meet` letterboxing
   - Isometric geometry from one `EDGE` constant; painter's algorithm via background-filled side faces
   - `agent-browser` CLI: `--session <name>`, `open`, `eval`, `screenshot`, `set viewport <w> <h>` (bare `viewport` is NOT a command)
   - `html { scroll-behavior: smooth }` breaks `window.scrollTo` in an `eval` — must set `document.documentElement.style.scrollBehavior='auto'` first
   - `codex exec -m gpt-5.6-luna -c model_reasoning_effort=high --yolo --skip-git-repo-check -C <dir> --add-dir <dir> -o <file>`; `--yolo` required for browser driving, must NOT be paired with `--full-auto`
   - Workflow tool `agent(prompt, {label, model, effort, phase, schema})` is the only way to set reasoning effort on a subagent
   - `lib/utils.ts` `cn()` is a plain filter+join, **no tailwind-merge** — conflicting classes resolve by CSS source order
   - RSC boundary rule: a `"use client"` module's exports are client references on the server (why `LEVEL_ALPHA` lives in `lib/activity-grid.ts`)
   - Vercel SSO deployment protection blocks the PR preview; critics audit `http://localhost:3001` (a local production build) instead

3. **Files and Code Sections:**

