content.text:
This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent:**

   The user's standing instruction (verbatim, carried from before compaction): **"Do all of them, complete each and every part, including the polish and optional ones. Make sure that the entire website is fully done and done with other details. Once you are done, then use the same subagent workflow critic to do the review again. by comparing our version (draft pr preview in browser) and chan dai's site in browser, using computer use."** Followed by **"continue....keep going"**, **"keep going! and continue"**, **"continue whats left and keep going!!!"**, and most recently **"status? continue please"**.

   Background intent: rebuild dhruv2mars.com in Chan Dai's (dai.is-a.dev / github.com/ncdai/chanhdai.com) design idiom with our own information architecture. Work lives on branch `feat/dai-idiom-rebuild`, draft PR **https://github.com/Dhruv2mars/portfolio/pull/36**. The user's original complaint was that the prior attempt "feels like as if someone has tried to copy from their own imagination without making sure that each and every part and detail are done exactly perfectly" — so every change must be made against **observed** Chan Dai source or **measured** browser state, never from memory.

2. **Key Technical Concepts:**
   - Next.js 16.2.10 App Router (Turbopack), React 19, TypeScript 5.8, Tailwind CSS v4, bun 1.3.13
   - Tailwind v4 `@utility`, `@theme inline`, `@custom-variant`, `@variant` nested inside `@utility`, `@apply` with opacity modifiers
   - `@custom-variant dark (&:where(.dark, .dark *));` at `app/globals.css:3`; `@custom-variant pointer-fine (@media (pointer: fine));` at line 6
   - Full-bleed decoration pattern: `absolute left-[-100vw] -z-1 w-[200vw]` (used by `screen-line-top`, `screen-line-bottom`, `stripe-divider`)
   - `Panel` already carries `screen-line-top screen-line-bottom border-x border-line`
   - `--line: color-mix(in oklab, var(--border) 64%, var(--background));` (globals.css:41); `--color-line: var(--line);` (line 131)
   - Fonts: `--font-sans: var(--font-geist-sans)`, `--font-mono: var(--font-geist-mono)`, `--font-heading: var(--font-sans)`, `--font-serif: var(--font-plex-serif)`, `--font-handwriting: var(--font-caveat)`
   - Chan Dai's footer grammar: tiled `grid gap-px bg-line` cells (1px gaps over a line-coloured ground) rather than bordered rows; `text-[0.625rem]/4 font-medium tracking-wider uppercase` micro-labels
   - Chan Dai's mobile command trigger: a SECOND button in a `fixed! bottom-[calc(--spacing(2)+env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0))] left-1/2 z-50 flex w-fit` wrapper; the desktop one is hidden via parent class `max-sm:*:data-[slot=command-menu-trigger]:hidden`
   - `agent-browser` CLI at `/Users/dhruv2mars/.bun/bin/agent-browser`: `--session <name>`, `open`, `eval`, `screenshot <abs-path>`, `set viewport <w> <h>` (bare `viewport` is NOT a command)
   - `html { scroll-behavior: smooth }` breaks `window.scrollTo` in an `eval` — must set `document.documentElement.style.scrollBehavior='auto'` first, in the same eval
   - `codex exec -m gpt-5.6-luna -c model_reasoning_effort=high --yolo --skip-git-repo-check -C <dir> --add-dir <dir> -o <file>`; must be launched directly from Bash with `run_in_background: true` (NOT via a relay subagent — see Errors)
   - `lib/utils.ts` `cn()` is a plain filter+join, **no tailwind-merge** — conflicting classes resolve by CSS source order
   - RSC boundary rule: a `"use client"` module's exports are client references on the server (why `LEVEL_ALPHA` lives in `lib/activity-grid.ts`)
   - Vercel SSO deployment protection blocks the PR preview; critics audit `http://localhost:3001` (a local production build) instead

3. **Files and Code Sections:**

   **`lib/ai-activity.ts`** — MODIFIED. The core data-honesty fix. Three edits:
   ```ts
   export type DailyTokens = {
     date: string;
     tokens: number;
     /**
      * Present, and `false`, only for days the feed never reached. A day measured
      * at zero and a day never measured are both "no tokens", but only the first
      * is a fact — the grid must not draw them the same. Absent means recorded,
      * so a series that is fully covered serialises exactly as it always did.
      */
     recorded?: false;
   };
   ```
   ```ts
   /**
    * Expand a sparse daily series into consecutive calendar days (0-filled gaps)
    * ending on `endDate`, keeping at most `windowDays` cells.
    *
    * Gaps *inside* the feed's coverage are real zeroes — the feed ran that day and
    * reported nothing. Days *past* its last report are not: they are marked
    * unrecorded so the grid can draw the difference.
    */
   export function fillSparseDailySeries(
     days: readonly DailyTokens[],
     endDate: string,
     windowDays = 365,
   ): DailyTokens[] {
     const byDate = new Map(days.map((d) => [d.date, d.tokens]));
     const covered = days.reduce((last, d) => (d.date > last ? d.date : last), "");
     const startDate = shiftYmd(endDate, -(windowDays - 1));
     const filled: DailyTokens[] = [];
     for (
       let cursor = startDate;
       cursor <= endDate;
       cursor = shiftYmd(cursor, 1)
     ) {
       filled.push(
         cursor <= covered
           ? { date: cursor, tokens: byDate.get(cursor) ?? 0 }
           : { date: cursor, tokens: 0, recorded: false },
       );
     }
     return filled;
   }
   ```
   `withLiveToday`'s docblock rules updated, and the stale-append branch became:
   ```ts
   appended.push({ date: cursor, tokens: 0, intensity: 0, recorded: false });
   ```
   Note: `materializeHistory` calls `fillSparseDailySeries(history, endHistory, 364)` where `endHistory` is the last history day, so history is always fully covered; the unrecorded days come from `withLiveToday`.

   **`components/activity-grid.tsx`** — MODIFIED (3 edits):
   ```tsx
   function cellLabel(day: ActivityDay): string {
     const date = formatActivityDate(day.date);
     // An unreported day has no number to read out. Saying "0 tokens" here would
     // put the same lie in the screen reader that a filled cell puts on screen.
     if (day.recorded === false) return `${date}: no data`;
     const tokens = `${formatTokenCount(day.tokens)} tokens`;
     return day.live ? `${date}: ${tokens} so far today` : `${date}: ${tokens}`;
   }
   ```
