This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent:**

   The only genuine user message in this segment: **"is the site fully done? if not, then continue"**.

   The standing instruction from the prior segment, still in force: **"continue and keep going until everything is utterly perfect and beautifully done. also, make sure whenever u shell out to codex with gpt5.6-luna-high, '@browser' will be used for it. so keep that in the prompt when sending."**

   And before that: **"Do all of them, complete each and every part, including the polish and optional ones. Make sure that the entire website is fully done and done with other details. Once you are done, then use the same subagent workflow critic to do the review again. by comparing our version (draft pr preview in browser) and chan dai's site in browser, using computer use."**

   Background intent: rebuild dhruv2mars.com in Chan Dai's design idiom (dai.is-a.dev) with our own information architecture. Branch `feat/dai-idiom-rebuild`, draft PR https://github.com/Dhruv2mars/portfolio/pull/36. **Every change must be made against observed Chan Dai source or measured browser state, never from memory** — the user's original complaint was that a prior attempt read as "a cheap copy by a five-year-old rather than an exact front end."

2. **Key Technical Concepts:**
   - Next.js 16.2.10 App Router (Turbopack), React 19, TypeScript 5.8, Tailwind CSS v4, bun 1.3.13
   - Tailwind v4 `@utility`, `@theme inline`, arbitrary variants, `h-(--custom-var)`, `--spacing(n)`
   - `lib/utils.ts` `cn()` is filter+join with **no tailwind-merge** — conflicting classes resolve by CSS source order
   - `agent-browser` CLI at `/Users/dhruv2mars/.bun/bin/agent-browser`: `--session <name>`, `set viewport`, `open`, `eval '<single expression>'`, `hover <sel>`, `screenshot <abs-path>`
   - `eval` needs ONE expression — wrap multi-statement code in an IIFE; re-declaring a `const` across evals in one session throws
   - `html { scroll-behavior: smooth }` breaks `window.scrollTo` in an eval — set `document.documentElement.style.scrollBehavior='auto'` in the SAME eval; scroll and dataset-read must be SEPARATE evals
   - `codex exec -m gpt-5.6-luna -c model_reasoning_effort=high --yolo --skip-git-repo-check -C /tmp/critique --add-dir /tmp/critique "$(cat prompt.txt)" > log 2>&1 < /dev/null &`
   - **Bash `run_in_background` returns exit 0 as soon as the `&`-detached wrapper exits — that notification does NOT mean codex finished.** Check with `pgrep -f "codex exec"`.
   - Codex's `@browser` skill is unavailable in headless `codex exec`; the prompt must explicitly frame `agent-browser` as the user-sanctioned browser surface or the run refuses with "no browser available"
   - Vercel SSO blocks the PR preview; critics audit `http://localhost:3001` (local production build, started with `PORT=3001 bun run start`)

