This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent:**

   **No new user messages arrived in this segment.** All work flowed from standing instructions carried forward from earlier segments:

   - Rebuild dhruv2mars.com in Chan Dai's design idiom (dai.is-a.dev) with the user's own information architecture, on branch `feat/dai-idiom-rebuild` / draft PR https://github.com/Dhruv2mars/portfolio/pull/36.
   - **Every change must be made against observed Chan Dai source or measured browser state, never from memory** — the original complaint was that a prior attempt read as "a cheap copy by a five-year-old rather than an exact front end."
   - "Do all of them, complete each and every part, including the polish and optional ones… Once you are done, then use the same subagent workflow critic to do the review again."
   - "continue and keep going until everything is utterly perfect and beautifully done. also, make sure whenever u shell out to codex with gpt5.6-luna-high, '@browser' will be used for it. so keep that in the prompt when sending."
   - Most recent explicit instruction (from the prior segment): **"then go ahead and do all. make sure everything is perfect and the whole site is looking and feeling utterly perfect"**

   A mid-conversation system-reminder (bypass permissions mode) instructed: prefer the Bash tool for reads/searches/edits (`cat`, `sed -n`, `grep`, heredocs, short scripts) over Read/Edit/Write, falling back to dedicated tools only when Bash genuinely cannot do the job.

2. **Key Technical Concepts:**
   - Next.js 16.2.10 App Router (Turbopack), React 19, TypeScript 5.8, Tailwind CSS v4, bun 1.3.13
   - `lib/utils.ts`'s `cn()` is a **plain join**, not tailwind-merge: later classes do NOT override earlier ones; stylesheet order decides.
   - Next.js file-based metadata: `app/icon.svg` → `<link rel="icon" href="/icon.svg?<hash>">`; `app/apple-icon.tsx` → `/apple-icon`; `app/manifest.ts` → `/manifest.webmanifest`.
   - `export const viewport: Viewport = { viewportFit: "cover" }` is required for `env(safe-area-inset-*)` to be non-zero on iOS.
   - satori/`ImageResponse` accepts `<img src="data:image/svg+xml;utf8,...">`; fonts must be passed explicitly (`fonts: [{name, weight, style, data}]`) — no font stack fallback exists. `new URL("./file.ttf", import.meta.url)` + `fetch` is the traced-asset pattern in the edge runtime.
   - `useSyncExternalStore(subscribe, getSnapshot, getServerSnapshot)` is the lint-clean way to read scroll position; the repo's eslint enforces `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect`.
   - Tailwind has no built-in `aria-current` variant — use arbitrary `aria-[current]:`.
   - `agent-browser` CLI (`/Users/dhruv2mars/.bun/bin/agent-browser`): `--session <name>`, `set viewport W H`, `set media dark|light`, `open`, `reload`, `eval '<ONE expression, IIFE>'`, `click <sel>`, `press`, `hover <sel>`, `type <sel> <text>`, `wait <ms>`, `console`, `errors`, `screenshot <abs-path>`, `mouse move/down/up`.
   - Reference uses next-themes with a stored preference: `set media dark` does not flip it; must `localStorage.setItem("theme","dark")` then reload.
   - SVG `className` is an object — use `String(el.className.baseVal ?? el.className)`.
   - Critics/verification audit `http://localhost:3001` (local production build via `PORT=3001 bun run start`) because Vercel SSO blocks the PR preview.
   - The harness blocks chained `sleep N; cmd`; use `for i in $(seq 1 N); do …; sleep 1; done`.
   - Critic invocation: `codex exec -m gpt-5.6-luna -c model_reasoning_effort=high --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox < /tmp/critique/roundN-prompt.md > /tmp/critique/roundN.log 2>&1`, prompt beginning with `@browser`.

3. **Files and Code Sections:**

   **`app/icon.svg`** — NEW. The favicon; the site previously had none at all.
   ```svg
