 * solves them. The page is prerendered and revalidates hourly, so the time
 * baked into the HTML can be an hour stale by the time it is served — a clock
 * that is visibly wrong for the moment before hydration is worse than no
 * clock. And the distance to the reader is a fact about the reader, which the
 * server cannot know at all.
