This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent:**

   Two user messages this segment, both governing.

   **User message 1:** "tell me whats the status? and how much we have achieved. how much %age is left before we can say, dhruv2mars.com is fully done and ready to be used." — answered with a status report (~92% done; five round-12 should-fix items; identity block blocked on the user).

   **User message 2 (the operative instruction):** "in my site, location, timezone will be additions other than the usual social/connect stuff. and just we will focus on the heatmap in future, not now. do the rest, once u are done with this sweep, open the dev server so that i can give u exact details and updates for fine tuning."

   Parsed as: (a) add **location** and **timezone** to the site as additions beyond the usual social/connect links; (b) the **heatmap/activity grid is deferred — do not touch it now** (this settles round-12 finding #2, the activity month-label typography, as out of scope); (c) **do everything else** in the round-12 sweep; (d) when the sweep is done, **start the dev server** so the user can supply exact details for fine-tuning.

   Standing instructions still in force from earlier segments:
   - Rebuild dhruv2mars.com in Chan Dai's design idiom (dai.is-a.dev) with the user's own information architecture, on branch `feat/dai-idiom-rebuild` / draft PR https://github.com/Dhruv2mars/portfolio/pull/36.
   - **Every change must be made against observed Chan Dai source or measured browser state, never from memory.**
   - "continue and keep going until everything is utterly perfect and beautifully done. also, make sure whenever u shell out to codex with gpt5.6-luna-high, '@browser' will be used for it. so keep that in the prompt when sending."
   - A bypass-permissions system-reminder: prefer the Bash tool for reads/searches/edits (`cat`, `sed -n`, `grep`, heredocs, short scripts) over Read/Edit/Write.
   - A SessionStart hook: CAVEMAN ULTRA communication mode always on.

   **Security constraints that must persist verbatim:** `rehype-sanitize` on all MDX (`components/mdx.tsx:4,111`) and escaped JSON-LD embedding via `serializeJsonLd` (`app/layout.tsx`, `app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx:76`) must survive the rebuild unchanged — regressing either is a security bug, not a style change. `isSafeHref` gating in `components/mdx.tsx` must be preserved. `BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN` and `AI_ACTIVITY_BLOB_URL` are environment variables consumed by `lib/ai-activity-store.ts` and must never be hardcoded. Data honesty rule: the fixture fallback renders identically but is labelled `fixture`; no data is ever invented. Vercel `ssoProtection` was deliberately NOT disabled — publishing the preview publicly is an outward-facing change requiring the user's consent.

2. **Key Technical Concepts:**
   - Next.js 16.2.10 App Router (Turbopack), React 19, TypeScript 5.8, Tailwind CSS v4, bun 1.3.13.
   - `lib/utils.ts`'s `cn()` is a **plain join**, not tailwind-merge: later classes do NOT override earlier ones; stylesheet order decides.
   - **A CSS `animation: X … reverse` does NOT restart an already-finished animation** — it re-reads the finished playhead against the other end of the timeline, so the element snaps to the far keyframe. An exit needs its own named keyframes.
   - **React unmounts synchronously**, so CSS `@starting-style` / `transition-behavior: allow-discrete` can never animate an exit; a presence hook must hold the node.
   - The repo's eslint enforces `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect`. The lint-clean escape is React's render-phase adjustment pattern (compare a previous value held in `useState`, call the setter during render), or `useSyncExternalStore`.
   - **An inline `<script dangerouslySetInnerHTML>` rendered inside the React client tree breaks hydration of `<html>`** — it made React revert `<html>`'s className, re-adding `.preload` and dropping `os-macos`.
