   - agent-browser `eval` round-trips take >100ms, so a 100ms animation is over before a second `eval` lands — measure entrance/exit inside **one** async IIFE with a `requestAnimationFrame` loop.
   - Verification target is `http://localhost:3001` (local production build via `PORT=3001 bun run start`) because Vercel SSO blocks the PR preview.
   - The harness blocks chained `sleep N; cmd`; use `for i in $(seq 1 N); do …; sleep 1; done`.
   - Do NOT run `bunx prettier` on this repo — it reformats at 80 columns and splits deliberate one-liners.

3. **Files and Code Sections:**

   **`app/globals.css`** — MODIFIED. Added `fade-out`, `palette-out`, `dock-sheet-in`, `dock-sheet-out` keyframes and the exit rules; extended the reduced-motion block.
   ```css
   @keyframes fade-in { from { opacity: 0; } to { opacity: 1; } }

   /* Written out rather than run as `fade-in … reverse`: reversing an animation
      that has already finished does not restart it, it re-reads the same finished
      playhead against the other end of the timeline — so the element snaps to the
      far keyframe instead of travelling to it. An exit needs its own name. */
   @keyframes fade-out { from { opacity: 1; } to { opacity: 0; } }
   ```
   ```css
   @keyframes palette-out {
     from { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
     to   { opacity: 0; transform: scale(0.95); }
   }

   /* The reference opens its dialog in a tenth of a second, from 95% and
      centred — no rise. …
      It leaves the same way. React unmounts a node the instant its state says so,
      which is why the exit needs `usePresence` to hold the node for the length of
      the animation — CSS alone, `@starting-style` included, never gets a frame. */
   .palette-panel { animation: palette-in 100ms var(--ease-out-quint) both; }
   .palette-panel[data-state="closed"] { animation: palette-out 100ms var(--ease-out-quint) both; }

   .palette-backdrop {
     animation: fade-in 160ms linear both;
     background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--background) 62%, transparent);
     backdrop-filter: blur(6px);
   }

