      the panel rather than outliving it: a dismissal that is still fading after
      the thing being dismissed has gone reads as lag. */
   .palette-backdrop[data-state="closed"] { animation: fade-out 100ms linear both; }

   /* ------------------------------------------------------------------
      Dock sheet

      The same tenth of a second as the palette, but it is not the same motion.
      The palette arrives centred, where the eye already is; the sheet arrives
      above a control at the foot of the screen, so it rises the 8px it is offset
      from that control and scales out of a point 8px *below* its own bottom edge
      — the dock button. It grows out of the thing that was pressed.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
   @keyframes dock-sheet-in {
     from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(8px) scale(0.95); }
     to   { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
   }
   @keyframes dock-sheet-out {
