This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent:**

   **Standing context (governs the whole session):** Rebuild dhruv2mars.com in Chan Dai's design idiom with the user's own information architecture, on branch `feat/dai-idiom-rebuild` / draft PR https://github.com/Dhruv2mars/portfolio/pull/36. Every change must be made against observed Chan Dai source (cloned at `/tmp/chanhdai` from `https://github.com/ncdai/chanhdai.com`) or measured browser state, never from memory. "continue and keep going until everything is utterly perfect and beautifully done. also, make sure whenever u shell out to codex with gpt5.6-luna-high, '@browser' will be used for it. so keep that in the prompt when sending." A bypass-permissions system-reminder directs preferring the Bash tool (`cat`, `sed -n`, `grep`, heredocs, short scripts) over Read/Edit/Write. CAVEMAN ULTRA communication mode is always on.

   **Security constraints that must persist verbatim:** `rehype-sanitize` on all MDX (`components/mdx.tsx`) and escaped JSON-LD embedding via `serializeJsonLd` (`app/layout.tsx`, `app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx`) must survive the rebuild unchanged — regressing either is a security bug, not a style change. `isSafeHref` gating in `components/mdx.tsx` must be preserved. `BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN`, `AI_ACTIVITY_BLOB_URL` and `AI_ACTIVITY_INGEST_SECRET` are environment variables consumed by `lib/ai-activity-store.ts` / `app/api/ai-activity/ingest/route.ts` and must never be hardcoded. Data honesty rule: no data is ever invented; unmeasured days must not be drawn as measured zeroes. Vercel `ssoProtection` was deliberately NOT disabled — publishing the preview publicly is an outward-facing change requiring the user's consent.

   **The operative request (user's most recent message):** the previous pass got many things wrong; use the real Chan Dai repo as reference. Specifically: (a) the navbar doesn't look like Chan's and "Projects" in nav isn't like Chan's — fix it; (b) "Projects" in the nav should open the new `/projects` page showing all projects, and the homepage projects "show more" should be like Chan's **but with the tilted arrow**, opening `/projects` on click; (c) all the same rules apply to **blogs**; (d) keep the footer like Chan's — **not below the "dhruv2mars" graphic** — keep it like it was before; only the tech-stack/colophon section was to be removed; (e) review the whole token activity section — the heatmap looks bad, cells have different sizes; (f) project rows feel weird on hover — refine; (g) "use emil skills to make sure everything is implemented correctly."

2. **Key Technical Concepts:**
   - Next.js 16.2.10 App Router (Turbopack), React 19, TypeScript 5.8, Tailwind CSS v4, bun 1.3.13.
   - Tailwind v4 already gates `hover:` behind `@media (hover: hover)`, satisfying the emil hover-gating rule; repo also defines `@custom-variant pointer-fine (@media (pointer: fine))`.
   - `lib/utils.ts`'s `cn()` is a plain join, not tailwind-merge — stylesheet order decides overrides.
